                <p class="card-link-copy">Quickler is job-agnostic. Send the pre-start, plant check or vehicle walkaround you already run and it becomes a WhatsApp workflow that asks each question in order, including the conditional follow-ups for a flagged item.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Faults that surface</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Red, amber, green at a glance</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">Every answer lands on the dashboard with a status colour, and photos and voice notes sit against the item they relate to. A defect on a harness or a cracked windscreen is visible the moment it is logged, not at the end of the week.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Anywhere a crew goes</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Town site or remote yard</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">It works anywhere WhatsApp does, so a crew on a rural site reports the same way as one in the city. Data is hosted on EU servers in Germany and handled in line with GDPR, with workflows in English today and more languages on the roadmap.</p>
            </article>
